{
  "contract": "fleet",
  "about": "Resolving routing policy from <dorkHome>/flow/fleet.json (spec flow-cli-core 1.1b). Call resolveFleetPolicy(accounts, fleet). input.accounts is the account list in runtime then registry order (a standalone default last), each { runtime, id, routable, implicit, isDefault? } from the account read (accounts.cases.json); isDefault absent reads as false for a registered account; input.fleet is the parsed fleet.json, or null when the file is missing. fleet.json accounts are keyed '<runtime>:<id>'. A bare key with no ':' was written before contract 2.0.0 and reads as 'claude-code:<key>'; when both forms are present the prefixed one wins ('entry-duplicate'). expected.accounts is one resolved policy per account, in input order, { runtime, id, key, role, reservePct, spendDownWindowHours, scope }, with every default filled in: role 'kept-out' for a registered account; for an implicit default (rev 6d): 'main' when its runtime has at least one ROUTABLE registered account and no account of that runtime has an explicit role 'main' in fleet.json, else 'rotation'; an explicit role always wins, reservePct 50 for main else 0, spendDownWindowHours 24, scope.repos []. A non-routable account always resolves to kept-out. At most one main per runtime: a later main of the same runtime reads as rotation ('main-duplicate'). expected.mains maps each runtime that has a main to its id. expected.handoff defaults to 'auto', expected.runtimes (the ordered runtime preference) to [] and expected.crossRuntimeFallback to 'off'; an invalid runtimes entry is dropped ('runtimes-invalid') and an unknown fallback reads as off ('cross-runtime-fallback-invalid'). expected.warnings is a multiset of codes (compare sorted). input.checks, when present, asks mayServe for an account (by key) and a checkout's origin URL (null = no origin): expected.checks gives, per check, the owner/name parsed from the origin (null when unparsable) and the mayServe answer. owner/name compare case-insensitively. Rev 6d aliases: when an account with isDefault true is NOT implicit (default is an alias of that row), an entry under '<runtime>:default' is that row's entry and is not reported as unknown; when the row's own key is also present, the row's own entry wins ('entry-duplicate'). A non-routable row that shares its key with a routable account (a hand-edited row with the reserved id 'default') does not warn 'entry-unroutable' for that entry.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "no fleet.json: every account is kept out",
      "input": {
        "accounts": [
          {"runtime": "claude-code", "id": "work", "routable": true, "implicit": false},
          {"runtime": "claude-code", "id": "claude3", "routable": true, "implicit": false}
        ],
        "fleet": null
      },
      "expected": {
        "handoff": "auto",
        "runtimes": [],
        "crossRuntimeFallback": "off",
        "mains": {},
        "accounts": [
          {
            "runtime": "claude-code",
            "id": "work",
            "key": "claude-code:work",
            "role": "kept-out",
            "reservePct": 0,
            "spendDownWindowHours": 24,
            "scope": {"repos": []}
          },
          {
            "runtime": "claude-code",
            "id": "claude3",
            "key": "claude-code:claude3",
            "role": "kept-out",
            "reservePct": 0,
            "spendDownWindowHours": 24,
            "scope": {"repos": []}
          }
        ],
        "warnings": []
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a complete policy, defaults filled in at read time",
      "input": {
        "accounts": [
          {"runtime": "claude-code", "id": "personal", "routable": true, "implicit": false},
          {"runtime": "claude-code", "id": "claude3", "routable": true, "implicit": false},
          {"runtime": "claude-code", "id": "org", "routable": true, "implicit": false},
          {"runtime": "claude-code", "id": "unlisted", "routable": true, "implicit": false}
        ],
        "fleet": {
          "v": 1,
          "handoff": "ask",
          "note": "unknown fields are ignored",
          "accounts": {
            "claude-code:personal": {"role": "main"},
            "claude-code:claude3": {"role": "rotation", "spendDownWindowHours": 12},
            "claude-code:org": {"role": "kept-out", "scope": {"repos": ["acme/app"]}}
          }
        }
      },
      "expected": {
        "handoff": "ask",
        "runtimes": [],
        "crossRuntimeFallback": "off",
        "mains": {"claude-code": "personal"},
        "accounts": [
          {
            "runtime": "claude-code",
            "id": "personal",
            "key": "claude-code:personal",
            "role": "main",
            "reservePct": 50,
            "spendDownWindowHours": 24,
            "scope": {"repos": []}
          },
          {
            "runtime": "claude-code",
            "id": "claude3",
            "key": "claude-code:claude3",
            "role": "rotation",
            "reservePct": 0,
            "spendDownWindowHours": 12,
            "scope": {"repos": []}
          },
          {
            "runtime": "claude-code",
            "id": "org",
            "key": "claude-code:org",
            "role": "kept-out",
            "reservePct": 0,
            "spendDownWindowHours": 24,
            "scope": {"repos": ["acme/app"]}
          },
          {
            "runtime": "claude-code",
            "id": "unlisted",
            "key": "claude-code:unlisted",
            "role": "kept-out",
            "reservePct": 0,
            "spendDownWindowHours": 24,
            "scope": {"repos": []}
          }
        ],
        "warnings": []
      }
    },
